course: dictionary
lesson: 502
title: Asphalt, tarmac and blacktop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Asphalt is a black, sticky material made by mixing small stones with bitumen. It is spread on roads, car parks and school playgrounds to make a hard surface for cars and people to use.
explain: Read the clues in this sentence: «At the bottom is hard-rolled crushed stone that spreads the weight of lorries, and on top is asphalt, a hot mix of small stones and sticky black bitumen, rolled flat while it is still warm.» The words hot mix, sticky and rolled flat tell you what asphalt is like.
explain: Asphalt can also be a verb. To asphalt means to cover a road or area with asphalt, so a council might asphalt a car park. The verb changes like other verbs: asphalts, asphalted, asphalting.
explain: People in different countries use other names for the same material. In the UK it is often called tarmac, in the US blacktop, and in Australia bitumen. When you read these words, check the sentence to see whether they mean the same thing as asphalt.
fact: «Asphalt» means a black, sticky material mixed with stones, used to make road surfaces and playgrounds.
fact: «To asphalt» means to cover a road or area with asphalt.
fact: Asphalt is put down hot and rolled flat while it is still warm.
fact: Asphalt gets hot in the sun, and falling on it can graze your knees.
fact: Tarmac (UK), blacktop (US) and bitumen (Australia) are other names people use for asphalt.
exercise: «At the bottom is hard-rolled crushed stone, and on top is asphalt, a hot mix of small stones and sticky black bitumen.» What is asphalt made of? | Ice and snow | Soft sand and water | *Small stones mixed with sticky black bitumen | Wood chips and glue
exercise: «A road roller squashes soil and hot asphalt flat with heavy steel drums.» What does the road roller do to the asphalt? | Carries it to school | Pours water on it | Digs a hole in it | *Squashes it flat
exercise: «Sam fell on the asphalt and grazed both knees.» What might have happened to Sam's knees? | They turned into stone | *They were scraped and sore | They grew longer | They were washed clean by the rain
test: In a car park, workers asphalt the ground. What does to asphalt mean? | Dig a hole | Wash a car | Paint a wall | *Cover an area with asphalt
test: «A road in America is covered in blacktop.» What is another name for blacktop? | Grass | *Asphalt | Gravel | Sand
exam: «The council will asphalt the playground next summer.» What kind of word is asphalt in this sentence? | *Verb | Adverb | Noun | Adjective
